  "the regreening of needless joy",
  "hello everyone.",
  "today i\u2019m fasting. well \u2014 i\u2019m on day three of a five-day fast.",
  "why am i fasting? i have no idea. the voice inside told me to, and i listened.",
  "i started thursday night around 10pm, and now it\u2019s sunday afternoon. so i\u2019m somewhere right in the middle of it. my nose is a little congested, but overall i feel pretty good. clear, even.",
  "one thing i\u2019m noticing is how fasting concentrates energy. i\u2019m moving slower, but more decidedly. more intentionally. my body feels\u2026 essentialized. like i\u2019m getting back in touch with who i am at a base level, without anything added. just water, salt, electrolytes. table salt, celtic salt. whatever the youtube doctors say is best.",
  "there\u2019s still an itchiness in my psyche i thought fasting might immediately clarify. maybe that comes later. maybe autophagy hasn\u2019t fully kicked in yet \u2014 whatever that really means. i\u2019m learning as i go.",
  "but i have had revelations.",
  "mostly, it\u2019s been about getting back in touch with my genuine soul. remembering why i came to this planet in the first place. and i keep arriving at the same thing: play.",
  "my mission has something to do with embracing the inner child. whimsy. joy. enjoying myself without justification. letting myself love what i love \u2014 disney songs, videos of people making soup, cleaning out the kitchen cabinet \u2014 whatever sparks delight in this particular here and now.",
  "i think the ultimate purpose of spirituality is liberation. and liberation, to me, is joyful. real freedom is being able to be joyful no matter what\u2019s happening around you. no matter who\u2019s grumpy, upset, throwing tantrums, or caught in their own weather systems.",
  "you don\u2019t have to get dragged into the unbearable fluctuations of the world. because the truth is: the world is impermanent. everything passes. pain doesn\u2019t last. happiness doesn\u2019t last. what people suffer over today won\u2019t be the same tomorrow. what people celebrate today will change too.",
  "joy is something deeper than happiness or sorrow. joy is the awareness of being itself. it doesn\u2019t even need a person. it\u2019s just\u2026 here.",
  "you\u2019re not a body that has awareness. you\u2019re awareness wearing a body. this temporary, beautiful instrument for exploring sensation, attachment, aversion, confusion, love. the body is a teacher.",
  "so whether you\u2019re fasting or feasting, exercising or exhausted, it doesn\u2019t really matter. the real question is: can you find joy here? can you touch the joy that\u2019s already present, regardless of circumstance?",
  "there are still things i want to do in this body. ideas i want to explore. but it\u2019s not about need. need is a survival word. when you know what you are \u2014 this divine everything, this divine nothing \u2014 you realize you need very little. maybe nothing at all.",
  "and from that place, you\u2019re free. free to be as you like. to do as you please. paradoxically, when you stop worrying, life leads you into the most joyful situations anyway.",
  "needless joy. that\u2019s what i want \u2014 for myself, and for others. though others are part of myself too. when i cultivate needless joy here, it ripples outward.",
  "i hear birds chirping outside my window. i feel spring approaching. a regreening. a reawakening. something soft and alive returning.",
  "fasting feels like a bodily metaphor for that \u2014 moving through winter into spring. letting yourself be empty so you can be full again. though emptiness and fullness aren\u2019t really so different. touch one deeply, and you find the other.",
  "so here\u2019s to needless joy, forever and always. happy new year!",
  "with infinite love,",
  "thank you",
